  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Scene Two and the ending"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "At home, Derry tells his mother he is going back to Mr Lamb's garden. She objects, saying people talk about Mr Lamb, but Derry insists, saying he has learnt to see things differently. When he returns, he finds that Mr Lamb has fallen from the ladder while picking crab apples and lies on the ground; it is understood that he has died. Derry kneels by him and weeps."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Derry defies his mother"
    },
    {
     "en": "He returns as promised"
    },
    {
     "en": "Mr Lamb has fallen from the ladder"
    }
   ],
