  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "title": {
    "en": "Value-based answer (80 words)"
   },
   "problem": {
    "en": "Why does Derry return to the garden even though his mother objects?"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "Mr Lamb treated him as a normal person."
    },
    {
     "en": "He has learnt to look at the world, not his face."
    },
    {
     "en": "He wants to keep his promise to help."
    },
    {
     "en": "His return shows a new confidence."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "Derry returns because Mr Lamb was the first person to treat him as normal and to show him a new way of seeing life. Keeping his promise matters to him. By defying his mother he shows new confidence: he has decided to stop hiding and to live among people."
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us build a model answer together. Why does Derry return to the garden even though his mother objects?"
   }
